{"kind":"artifact","text":"go.mod at exact clean pushed head 62d1f6a3c519249850f67278e2df634a50d7042a on request/go126-security-patch, answering 644b97c62b. This is the implementation report for that request.\n\nThe change is one line: the go directive moves from 1.26.0 to 1.26.7. Nothing else changed. No dependency moved, no toolchain line was added, no code was touched. git diff against the base is one file, one insertion, one deletion.\n\nWhy that line is the fix. ci.yml, security.yml and performance.yml all resolve their toolchain with go-version-file: go.mod, so the directive is what selects the standard library CI compiles and scans against. The advisories in Security run 32670745689 are all standard-library, so raising the directive is the whole repair.\n\nThe toolchain actually used was go1.26.7, not the 1.26.5 installed here. GOTOOLCHAIN is auto, and go printed \"downloading go1.26.7 (darwin/arm64)\" before reporting \"go version go1.26.7 darwin/arm64\"; go env GOVERSION agrees. I checked that rather than assume the directive was honoured.\n\nAdvisories, measured before and after rather than inferred from the version string. Before, on a pristine checkout of the base, the exact workflow command exited 3 and reported six reachable standard-library advisories at symbol level: GO-2026-6218 in net/url, reached from host/identity/github.go 99 through http.Client.Do to url.URL.Parse; GO-2026-6091 in html/template, reached from internal/perfscenario/run.go 736; GO-2026-6090 in crypto/tls, four traces including cmd/gs/main.go 2137 through http.Server.Serve; GO-2026-6089 in net/http from the same line; GO-2026-5972 in encoding/asn1, reached from internal/app/app.go 1238; and GO-2026-5026, the x/net/idna Punycode failure reached through net/http from host/identity/github.go 99. Every one is fixed in go1.26.6, so 1.26.7 covers them. After the change the same command exits 0 and reports no vulnerabilities.\n\nTwo further advisories existed before at import level only, where the code does not call the vulnerable symbols: GO-2026-6088 in encoding/xml and GO-2026-5942 in net. Both are standard-library and both are also fixed in go1.26.6, so they are gone too. I separate them because they were never reachable, and a summary that folded them in with the six would overstate what was repaired.\n\nGates at the pushed head, all exit zero: go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test ./... -count=1 across thirty packages with no failures, and the exact command security.yml runs, go run golang.org/x/vuln/cmd/govulncheck@v1.1.4 ./....\n\nWhat this does not establish. The govulncheck runs measured this machine's fetched go1.26.7 toolchain, not the runner image CI will install; the mechanism is the same go-version-file resolution, but I have not watched the hosted workflow go green at this head. Nothing here was inferred from a check that did not run.","body":{"commit":"62d1f6a3c519249850f67278e2df634a50d7042a","path":"go.mod"}}